cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "nof1kit: Design, Monitor, and Analyze Single-Case (N-of-1) Intensive Longitudinal Studies"
message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
type: software
authors:
  - given-names: Miura
    family-names: Meng
    email: haomeng797@gmail.com
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0009-0004-1522-1997"
    affiliation: "University of Pennsylvania"
repository-code: "https://github.com/haomeng797-ship-it/nof1kit"
url: "https://haomeng797-ship-it.github.io/nof1kit/"
abstract: >-
  Covers the stages of a single-case (N-of-1) experimental study that come
  before analysis. Randomization schedules are drawn uniformly from the set of
  sequences satisfying a run-length constraint, by counting valid completions
  from each state with dynamic programming rather than by rejection sampling,
  which is unworkable at realistic study lengths. Schedules export as plain
  JSON for a mobile collection layer, incoming ecological momentary assessment
  records are checked for out-of-range values, duplicate timestamps and day
  indices that have drifted out of step with the calendar, and compliance is
  counted as scheduled prompts answered inside their response window. A
  simulation-based power function reports how much a design can detect with
  and without an AR(1) error structure, since whether ignoring serial
  dependence is conservative or anti-conservative depends on the schedule.
keywords:
  - single-case design
  - N-of-1 trials
  - ecological momentary assessment
  - randomization
  - intensive longitudinal data
  - research infrastructure
  - R
license: MIT
version: 0.1.0
